      "text": "To find the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome, we need to manipulate the digits of the number \\( 5678 \\) in such a way that we can find a smaller value for \\( x \\) and still make the number a palindrome.\n\nFirst, we separate the digits of \\( 5678 \\):\n\\[\n5, 6, 7, 8\n\\]\nWe start by forming the largest palindrome that can be subtracted from \\( 5678 \\). The largest palindrome less than \\( 5678 \\) is formed by adding the largest possible digits:\n\\[\n8, 7, 6, 5 \\rightarrow 5, 6, 7, 8\n\\]\nThus, the largest possible palindrome less than \\( 5678 \\) is \\( 5678 - 2 = 5676 \\), because \\( 7 \\) by itself cannot form a larger palindrome and adding any digit greater than \\( 7 \\) would exceed \\( 5678 \\).\n\nWe verify this:\n\\[\n5678 - 5676 = 2\n\\]\nThis results in \\( 2 \\), which is not a palindrome.\n\nNext, we verify the largest possible smaller palindrome. The largest possible smaller palindrome can be formed by swapping two digits in \\( 5678 \\):\n\\[\n7, 6, 8, 5 \\rightarrow 5, 8, 6, 7\n\\]\nThis results in:\n\\[\n5678 - 5867 = -2\n\\]\nThis is not a valid palindrome and does not fit our criteria.\n\nGiven that we need a new approach, let's try incrementing smaller entities in the structure:\n\\[\n71, 61, 81, 51 \\rightarrow 5, 6, 7, 8\n\\]\nShould be:\n\\[\n5678 - 71 = 5607\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n6, 5, 6, 7 \\rightarrow 5, 6, 7, 8 \n\\]\nReplace digits to match 5, 6, 7, 8, resulting in:\n\\[\n8, 6, 7, 5 + 2 \\rightarrow 5678 - 2 = 5674\n\\]\nThus, the smallest \\( x \\) is:\n\\[\nx = 58\n\\]\nThus, the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{58}\n\\]",
